From: "mach-choice lane (C1)" <fleet@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] blazer: the Synaptics TouchComm touch screen (hakios.tcm), integrated-tree form

Applies to the blazer integrated tree
(research/laguna-foundation/kernel-blazer/xnu-src/xnu-8796.121.2) on top of
0001-blazer-r4r5-laguna-evidence-chain.patch (order not load-bearing).

Source: research/laguna-touch/patches/0001-blazer-*.patch (host suite
198/198), with three kernel-build fixes this lane had to make — the fleet
patch only ever compiled host-side (HAKIOS_TCM_HOSTTEST), which compiled the
kernel section out:
  1. bsd/dev/hakios.tcm.c included sys/hakios.input.h before the kernel
     types existed (bool/dev_t unknown) — the include now follows the
     libkern/systm block, the same order hakios.goodix.c uses.
  2. kern/misc_protos.h is not in the bsd pass's include set here (it wants
     vprintf) — sys/systm.h, included above, declares vprintf.
  3. the kernel section's statics tcm_bus_write/read/attn collided with the
     unconditional generic wrappers of the same names (static redefinition);
     renamed to tcm_kernel_write/read/attn and wired through the generic
     indirection (hakios_tcm_bus = tcm_kernel_bus at init, unchanged).
Host suite re-run against the patch form: PASS (TouchComm v2 identify,
panel 1280x2856, touch reports ready).

